id: pm-wdrkfr
title: "GH-708: make retained delete tombstones discoverable and policy-controlled"
description: "Expose history streams retained after pm delete as intentional tombstones through supported health/list output, explain retention in delete results/help, and define explicit opt-in retention or garbage-collection policy without weakening append-only audit defaults."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[9]: agent-ux,"area:history","area:storage",delete,gc,gh-issue,"gh:unbraind/pm-cli#708",multi-agent,observability
created_at: "2026-07-25T12:10:49.472Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-25T12:38:49.342Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "pm health or an equivalent supported command reports a bounded count/list of history streams without live item files and distinguishes valid delete tombstones from corruption; pm delete output and help explicitly state that the history stream is retained; an opt-in tombstone retention or gc policy is documented and cannot silently remove append-only proof; SDK/CLI contracts expose the same structured tombstone state; sandboxed delete, health, history, gc, and merge regression tests preserve 100% coverage"
objective: "Deleted-item audit streams are visible, explainable, and bounded by an explicit retention policy"
value: Agents can distinguish intentional audit proof from orphaned residue and can manage long-lived multi-agent workspace growth without raw filesystem inspection
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: medium
confidence: high
